// A method NAMED without being called. kama has no bound-method values (a method is reached through a
// `BindableFunctionPtr`, spelled `Type::method`), so a bare `v.m` is a call missing its parentheses —
// say so, rather than "no field", which sends the reader looking for a field that was never wanted.
type value V {
    public int32 n;
    public ctor make() { this.n = 1; }
    public fn int32 m() { return this.n; }
}
fn int32 main() { V v = V.make(); return v.m; }   // ERROR: `v.m` names a method — call it (`v.m(...)`)
